# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this React + Vite project following the official Vercel documentation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Installed Dependencies
- Added `@vercel/analytics` package (version 2.0.1)
- Package installed using npm
- Updated `package-lock.json` with new dependencies

### 2. Modified Files

**frontend/package.json**
- Added `@vercel/analytics` to dependencies

**frontend/src/App.jsx**
- Imported `Analytics` component from `@vercel/analytics/react`
- Added `<Analytics />` component to the App component's JSX
- Placed the Analytics component at the end of the root fragment for optimal loading

### 3. Implementation Details
According to the latest Vercel Analytics documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), for React/Vite projects:
- The Analytics component should be imported from `@vercel/analytics/react`
- The component should be added to the root App component
- No additional configuration is required for basic setup

### 4. Verification
- ✅ Build completed successfully (client + SSR)
- ✅ No linting errors (no linter configured in project)
- ✅ No test failures (no tests configured in project)
- ✅ Package-lock.json updated with new dependencies

## Notes
- The Analytics component will automatically track page views when deployed to Vercel
- The component is lightweight and loads asynchronously to avoid impacting performance
- Build artifacts (dist-server/entry-server.js) were not staged as they are generated files
- The implementation follows the official documentation's framework-specific instructions for React/Vite
